<anchor xml:id="_class_assimp_1_1_export_properties_1abcb151b5c3da6c759b13b6f25abe65c9"/><section>
    <title>GetPropertyBool()</title>
<indexterm><primary>GetPropertyBool</primary><secondary>Assimp::ExportProperties</secondary></indexterm>
<indexterm><primary>Assimp::ExportProperties</primary><secondary>GetPropertyBool</secondary></indexterm>
<para><computeroutput>bool Assimp::ExportProperties::GetPropertyBool (const char * szName, bool bErrorReturn = <computeroutput>false</computeroutput>
) const<computeroutput>[inline]</computeroutput></computeroutput></para>
<para>Get a boolean configuration property. Boolean properties are stored on the integer stack internally so it&apos;s possible to set them via <link linkend="_class_assimp_1_1_export_properties_1a3eb3aea4da6b94da06b7dd118c864c38">SetPropertyBool</link> and query them with <link linkend="_class_assimp_1_1_export_properties_1abcb151b5c3da6c759b13b6f25abe65c9">GetPropertyBool</link> and vice versa. <formalpara><title>See also</title>

<para><link linkend="_class_assimp_1_1_export_properties_1a24257a57419d1f143cde1221c2300ecb">GetPropertyInteger()</link> </para>
</formalpara>
</para>
</section>
